WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:04.770
Sefton Delmer was a writer who created “Black
Propaganda” on behalf of the British government,

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.990
and used “fake news” to fight the Nazi
regime.

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:12.309
Through postcards, court documents, and pirate
radio programs, Delmer and the rest of the

00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:16.780
secret service infiltrated the minds of the
German people, using elements of violence,

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:21.480
sex, and death in their stories to subtlety
break down the morale of the Nazis.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.310
So, who was Sefton Delmer?

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:28.710
And why was he most likely the only man on
Earth who could have become the true master

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.779
of Black Propaganda?

00:00:31.779 --> 00:00:45.480
Early Life and Career
Denis Sefton Delmer was born in 1904 in Berlin,

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:46.480
Germany.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.680
As a child, everyone called him “Tom”,
but as an adult, everyone remembered him by

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.420
his parent’s conjoined last names, and he
was known as “Sefton Delmer”.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.600
His father, Frederick Sefton Delmer, taught
English at Berlin University.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:01.800
His parents were both from Australia, and
they had Jewish heritage.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.990
They registered his birth at the British Consulate,
so that he could be a dual citizen.

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:11.440
He only spoke German before the age of 5,
which is parents chose to do on purpose, hoping

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:12.560
he would blend in better.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.860
He grew up to become bilingual in both English
and German, but his parents still raised him

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:19.790
to understand his Australian ancestry at home.

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:24.260
At the start of World War I, his Father Frederick
was removed from his position as a professor

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:28.710
at the university, because he was a so-called
“enemy alien”, and he was forced to live

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.540
at the Ruhleben Internment Camp.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:34.470
Growing up in Germany, the other children
in school labeled him as an enemy, and he

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:38.770
was isolated from his peers and bullied for
being different, even though they were exactly

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:40.040
the same.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.920
In 1917, Frederick was released from the camp
through a prisoner exchange program between

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.140
the British and the Germans, but instead of
going back to Australia, the whole family

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.370
was deported to England.

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:53.240
So, Sefton Delmer was able to transfer to
a school in London.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:57.070
Since German was his first language, he couldn’t
help but speak with an accent.

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:01.020
As far as his English classmates were concerned,
he was considered the “enemy” once again,

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.150
and he was also isolated from the other children
in school.

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:07.990
Even though this must have been difficult,
this life of being stuck in-between two worlds

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:12.299
is precisely why he was able to understand
both cultures so completely.

00:02:12.299 --> 00:02:16.430
Since he was ostracized for the sound of his
voice, or the words he used, it only made

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:22.349
him pay attention to those details more, and
it would all come in handy later on in his

00:02:22.349 --> 00:02:23.620
adult life.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:27.870
World War I ended in 1918, when Sefton Delmer
was 14 years old.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:32.370
Despite the fact that he had endured so much
bullying in his younger years, he still embraced

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.099
the fact that he was bilingual.

00:02:34.099 --> 00:02:38.159
He went on to study Oxford University, where
he studied German, possibly to follow in his

00:02:38.159 --> 00:02:40.790
father’s footsteps of securing a job as
a professor.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:43.749
However, he never did start a teaching career.

00:02:43.749 --> 00:02:48.469
He was able to fully embrace the other passion
in his life, writing.

00:02:48.469 --> 00:02:52.790
And this was just the beginning of his destiny.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:03:00.519
Life Before the War
After graduating from Oxford University, Sefton

00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:03.760
Delmer got a job for a magazine called The
Daily Express.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:07.790
Since he was bilingual, he became very valuable
to the magazine in translating the news coming

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.790
out of Germany, in order to make the British
public aware.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:15.400
He was able to become friendly with the Nazi
officer Ernst Rohm, who introduced him to

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.319
Adolf Hitler in 1932.

00:03:17.319 --> 00:03:21.370
At this time, Hitler had actually lost his
first election, and he would not become Chancellor

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:23.659
of Germany until 1933.

00:03:23.659 --> 00:03:27.480
Sefton Delmer was able to travel with Hitler
on his private plane, and listen to all of

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:30.349
his plans for what he wanted for Germany.

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:33.840
He became the first British journalist to
ever secure an interview with Adolf Hitler,

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:38.609
and he traveled to Berlin to report the day
when he took office in 1933.

00:03:38.609 --> 00:03:43.120
This may seem like a monumental event that
should have set him off right then and there,

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:47.849
but at the time, no one would ever predict
that Hitler would become an evil dictator.

00:03:47.849 --> 00:03:52.170
He was promising to bring Germany out of the
financial hardships it had endured after World

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:57.089
War I. and he was even given the title of
“Man of the Year” in Time Magazine.

00:03:57.089 --> 00:04:01.989
So, as far as The Daily Express was concerned,
there were far more important things to focus

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:02.989
on.

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:06.250
That same year, The Daily Express sent him
to France to work out of their offices in

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:07.250
Paris.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:10.760
At that time, Paris was the place to be for
some of the most creative people in history.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:15.019
Some of the most famous writers of that time
were all living and working there in the late

00:04:15.019 --> 00:04:19.709
1920’s to early 1930’s, and many of them
were actually friends with one another, as

00:04:19.709 --> 00:04:20.709
well.

00:04:20.709 --> 00:04:23.900
These writers were apart of the so-called
“lost generation”, and they indulged heavily

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:26.340
in drugs, sex, and jazz.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:31.190
While in Paris, Sefton Delmer met and fell
in love with a woman named Isabel Nicholas.

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:33.979
She was a very successful artist, designer,
and model.

00:04:33.979 --> 00:04:38.970
She was quite beautiful, and she became the
muse for several famous painters and sculptors,

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:39.970
including Pablo Picasso.

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:45.250
In a lot of ways, they were a perfect match
for one another, and in 1935, the two were

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:46.250
married.

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:50.080
A couple years later, Sefton Delmer became
a correspondent during the Spanish Civil War,

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:53.560
which lasted from 1936 to 1939.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.740
General Francisco Franco was trying to take
over the Spanish government on behalf of Fascism,

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:03.439
and both Nazi Germany and Italy were sending
money and ammunition to Franco’s army.

00:05:03.439 --> 00:05:07.979
Sefton Delmer became good friends with Ernest
Hemingway, who was there writing the script

00:05:07.979 --> 00:05:11.610
and did the voiceover for a documentary called
The Spanish Earth.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:15.000
Another writer, Martha Gellhorn, was also
there for Collier’s Magazine.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.569
She was one of the only female war correspondents.

00:05:17.569 --> 00:05:21.620
She was also willing to put her life in danger
to get the scoop on a story.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:25.569
She would later get married to Hemingway,
making her his third wife.

00:05:25.569 --> 00:05:29.871
A large group of these writers, photographers,
and filmmakers lived together in the Hotel

00:05:29.871 --> 00:05:35.130
Florida in Madrid, and they were often singing
and drinking in the hotel lobby and bar.

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:38.800
They all believed that by covering the events
of the Spanish Civil War, they could shed

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:43.099
light on the fact that Adolf Hitler was already
pushing his Fascist regime on the rest of

00:05:43.099 --> 00:05:46.379
the world, and that the Nazis were dangerous.

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:50.750
But these writers would have no idea that
soon enough, their own countries would be

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:55.770
at war as well, and there was nothing they
could do to stop it.

00:05:55.770 --> 00:06:02.379
Black Propaganda
On the brink of World War II, secret agents

00:06:02.379 --> 00:06:04.860
and spies were commonplace throughout Europe.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:08.930
Her Majesty’s Secret Service was paying
close attention to anyone they believed could

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:12.419
be a Nazi sympathizer, including Sefton Delmer.

00:06:12.419 --> 00:06:17.379
It was like he was living through his elementary
school experience again, because the Germans

00:06:17.379 --> 00:06:22.060
believed that he was an agent for MI6, and
they no longer allowed him to interview Adolf

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:25.290
Hitler or any other high-ranking member of
the Nazi party.

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:28.979
It was only after he returned to London and
started working for the German branch of the

00:06:28.979 --> 00:06:32.810
BBC that the British government knew they
could actually trust him.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:37.730
Sefton Delmer once described one of Adolf
Hitler’s speeches as coming from his “lying,

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:38.730
stinking teeth”.

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:43.259
While that’s not exactly the most professional
thing a journalist can say on the air, it

00:06:43.259 --> 00:06:48.360
actually worked out really well for him, because
in 1940, he was recruited by the Political

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:51.689
Warfare Executive branch, or the PWE’s for
short.

00:06:51.689 --> 00:06:56.419
A that time, the British secret service was
very concerned about a pirate radio program

00:06:56.419 --> 00:07:01.310
called “Worker’s Challenge” was broadcasting
from inside of the UK, but it was actually

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:05.780
a German propaganda show run by talented actors
who spoke fluent English.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:10.350
They were posing as an anti-war program, and
they spread fake news to bring down the morale

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:11.530
of the British troops.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:16.150
The British government asked Delmer to make
his own version of a radio show that was “Black

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:17.150
Propaganda”.

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:21.969
The goal was to give out roughly 80% real
facts, but try to slip in 20% fake news that

00:07:21.969 --> 00:07:23.870
was meant to subvert the Germans.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:28.409
He wholeheartedly agreed to do the job, and
his wife, Isabel, was excited to help in whatever

00:07:28.409 --> 00:07:29.569
way she could, as well.

00:07:29.569 --> 00:07:34.370
In 1941, the government gave him a requisitioned
country house in Bedfordshire, where he worked

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.810
together with a team on creating propaganda.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:41.189
Isabel illustrated fake postcards of German
soldiers with French prostitutes.

00:07:41.189 --> 00:07:45.639
This was meant to make French men angry and
jealous, and inherently dislike the Nazis.

00:07:45.639 --> 00:07:53.810
At that time, Isabel’s illustrations were
sexy and suggestive, but far from being pornorgraphic.

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:58.189
Sefton Delmer started a radio broadcast, and
he wrote scripts under the alias of “Der

00:07:58.189 --> 00:07:59.189
Chef”.

00:07:59.189 --> 00:08:03.139
He hired a German immigrant and actor named
Paul Saunders to be the voice of the character.

00:08:03.139 --> 00:08:07.639
He spoke with a perfect Berlin accent, and
they had a strong enough radio tower to make

00:08:07.639 --> 00:08:10.650
it seem as if the show was being broadcast
from Germany.

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:15.379
Der Chef claimed to be a loyal Nazi, and that
he was simply giving insider information to

00:08:15.379 --> 00:08:17.039
inform his fellow comrades.

00:08:17.039 --> 00:08:20.870
He used coarse language, and spoke out against
the enemies of the Third Reich.

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:25.259
Since Delmer grew up in Germany, he knew how
to write like these words were truly coming

00:08:25.259 --> 00:08:29.580
from a German person, and no one would have
ever known that the show was actually produced

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:30.580
by the English.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:34.600
Sefton Delmer had a great sense of humor,
and he knew how to capture an audience’s

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:35.600
attention.

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:39.380
Much of the fake news he wrote included sexual
stories, which was enough to keep the audience

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:41.090
listening on a regular basis.

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:44.510
For example, he once wrote that the British
were trying to get German prisoners of war

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:48.320
to give up their secrets by tying them up
and “torturing” them with strippers.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:51.760
Der Chef urged them to be strong, and not
give in to temptation.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:55.790
Saunders would have to tell these stories
as if he was outraged at the English, saying,

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:58.210
“Don’t give in to these perversions!

00:08:58.210 --> 00:08:59.210
Say nothing!”

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:02.240
Then, once he had their attention, he would
go on to tell fake news that was secretly

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.270
meant to demoralize the enemy.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:08.540
Sefton Delmer was also apart of the government’s
“Underground Propaganda Committee”.

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:12.910
It was their job to collect rumors that were
already spreading in German communities, and

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:15.750
used those as the basis of their fake news.

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:20.330
By using this strategy, they were simply confirming
what people were already whispering about,

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:24.670
so it was far easier to the audience to believe
that it was true.

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:28.730
Along with the “Der Chef” show, Sefton
Delmer wrote and produced a second radio program

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:32.860
called “Atlantic Sender”, which was meant
to seduce German soldiers.

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:36.020
They played jazz music, which had been forbidden
to German citizens.

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:41.180
A female actress named ç, who they called
“Vicky”, read the scripts in her sultry

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.180
voice.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:45.720
Together with another writer and spy, Ian
Fleming, Delmer put together stories that

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:51.510
were basically erotic fan fiction of various
fantasy scenarios between German men and English

00:09:51.510 --> 00:09:52.510
women.

00:09:52.510 --> 00:09:54.870
These stories worked exactly as he had hoped
they would.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:59.260
A former German officer named Horst Bredo
said that he would listen to “Atlantic Sender”

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:01.310
with the rest of the men who were stationed
in a U-Boat.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:04.950
Once he saw the photographs of how truly beautiful
the actress was, he asked for a copy of photos,

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:09.810
and joked, “If there were TV’s on board
the U-Boat, and we saw these pictures, a lot

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:12.020
of them would say, ‘The war is finished.

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:14.520
Let’s go home and be with English girls.’”

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:17.550
Of course, not everyone was a fan of these
sexy stories.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:21.730
A politician named Sir Stafford Cripps got
ahold of an English translation of the Der

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:22.880
Chef broadcast.

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:27.630
The particular script he read was a dirty
story about an orgie, and Cripps was disgusted

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:28.910
by how crude they were.

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:32.280
He wrote, “If this is how we win the war,
I’d rather lose it.”

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:35.480
Despite receiving this criticism, the show
was able to continue.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:39.910
The Black Propaganda team had really figured
out what made men tick, and their subversive

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:45.130
messages manipulating me through their sexual
desires and fantasies was actually working.

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:50.540
Years later, after the war was won, Delmer’s
co-writer, Ian Fleming, had a lightbulb moment.

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:55.230
If the German soldiers would go crazy fantasizing
over these characters, so would the rest of

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:56.330
the men in the world.

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:59.980
He continue to write these sexy stories, only
this time, the main character was a British

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:03.690
spy, whose adventures were based on his own
experiences during the war.

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:06.930
He wrote pulp fiction novels about his alter-ego,
James Bond.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:11.590
Delmer’s wife, Isabel, would later say that
they were both having the time of their lives

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:13.140
creating this propaganda.

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:16.770
She thought it was hilarious that the government
was essentially paying her to draw pornography

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:17.770
for a living.

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:21.720
They recruited some of the most talented artists
in the country to join the team, and Sefton

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:25.350
Delmer had his own sense of humor for initiating
new recruits.

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:29.670
A 22-year old artist named Marion Whitehorn
was asked to join the secret organization.

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:32.980
There were several British generals there
the day of her briefing.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:36.700
They were all wearing their uniforms, without
even a hint of a smile on their faces.

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:40.060
Delmer said that if she told anyone about
the secret mission they were about to give

00:11:40.060 --> 00:11:43.930
her, she would be sent to jail, and suffer
10 years of hard labor.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:48.020
She nervously agreed, and he slid a postcard
of Adolf Hitler across the table.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:52.050
The postcard was titled with the German phrase;
“What we have, we hold”.

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:56.420
Her first assignment was to tamper the postcard
to make it look as though Hitler was holding

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:58.180
his own penis in his hand.

00:11:58.180 --> 00:12:02.130
Decades later, Marion Whitehorn told this
story during an interview for a documentary.

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:06.490
She said, looking back, she could have laughed,
but the atmosphere of the room was so serious,

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:09.690
she simply agreed to do the duty for her country.

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:14.260
As she left the room to get started, Sefton
Delmer called out, “But not too big, Marion!”

00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:18.440
Meanwhile, in Germany, the Nazi Minister of
Propaganda, Joseph Goebbels, had an entirely

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:19.800
different strategy all together.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:24.590
Instead of using subtle and creative writing,
he was loud, and confidently stated bold lies

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:27.910
about how the Jews were to blame for Germany’s
hardships.

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:32.150
For a population of people who were desperate,
they clung on to the idea that they could

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:35.020
blame the Jews for the economic problems of
Germany.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:38.960
As time went on, it became clear to Sefton
Delmer and his team that writing subtle jokes

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:42.300
and sexy stories were not going to be enough
to win the war.

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:44.190
So, they had to get darker.

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:49.040
Delmer’s team was able to find the exact
typeface used in official German documents.

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:52.810
This way, they created fake court records,
and “leaked” them to the public.

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:57.320
All of these fictional court cases were made
to have the S.S. Officers guilty of rape and

00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:58.320
murder.

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:01.800
He wrote excruciating details of the story,
only to have them acquitted of all charges

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:02.800
by the end.

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:06.271
This was obviously meant to outrage anyone
who read the documents, and it made the Nazi

00:13:06.271 --> 00:13:08.640
government look like complete monsters.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:13.230
He wrote these to try to convince German people
that they were fighting for an evil, corrupt

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:14.230
government.

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:17.690
In 1943, he decided that he wanted to stop
the “Der Chef” broadcast, but he knew

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:22.110
that his character would never actually stop
his radio broadcast, unless he was forced

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:23.110
to.

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:26.790
So he wrote and staged a scene where Nazi
soldiers came through the door to his studio,

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:28.570
and shot him while he was live on air.

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:32.320
He hoped that if Nazi soldiers were out there
listening, they would realize that there was

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:37.320
no such thing as freedom of the press in a
Fascist government.

00:13:37.320 --> 00:13:44.120
Psychological Warfare
The longer the war went on, the higher the

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:45.120
stakes became.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:48.850
They felt that it was necessary to mess with
the the minds of German men in the darkest

00:13:48.850 --> 00:13:49.850
ways.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:52.810
A lot of the information that was given to
the Black Propaganda writers came directly

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:57.830
from highly skilled British Intelligence agents
who were interrogating captured Nazi soldiers.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:01.530
Whenever a Nazi soldier refused to say anything
about his top-secret information, they would

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:05.130
try to get him to relax and talk about his
personal life, instead.

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:08.640
Without realizing it, these soldiers were
giving up information about the bases where

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:12.190
they were staying, the bars where German soldiers
drank, and so on.

00:14:12.190 --> 00:14:15.960
So, since those names and details given out
about these men on the radio were accurate,

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:20.640
they believed there must be a spy among them
who was giving away all of their information.

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:24.330
This made the Germans distrust one another,
and it was difficult for them to form a close

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:26.250
bond with their comrades.

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:30.290
They would read out the names of streets that
had been apparently bombed in Berlin and Hamburg,

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:31.290
even if they hadn’t.

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:35.030
They purposely figured out where German U-Bombers
lived, so that they could read out the specific

00:14:35.030 --> 00:14:37.410
addresses of all of the men who were on the
boats.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:41.050
This would make the soldiers fall into a state
of depression and anxiety, and completely

00:14:41.050 --> 00:14:42.370
ruin their morale.

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:46.210
Many of those German soldiers would go through
the rest of the war feeling like they had

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:47.240
nothing to fight for.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:51.340
The British also dropped photographs of dead
women and children over German bases, which

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:54.780
made them wonder if their own wives and children
were among the dead.

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:58.450
Many of these men would be in the shock of
their lives to go home to find out that their

00:14:58.450 --> 00:15:00.700
family was actually still alive.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:05.230
The Germans chose to do the same sort of propaganda,
only with the strategy to make the Allied

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:07.660
soldiers want to end the war and go home.

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:11.860
They played on men’s jealousies, with a
sultry female voice playing over the radio,

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:15.270
asking if they knew what their wives and girlfriends
were doing without them.

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:20.320
By the time Americans joined the war, German
planes were dropping leaflets of fake “Life”

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:24.700
magazines featuring photographs of nude women
on one side, and “Death” with a skull

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:26.090
wearing a helmet on the other.

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:31.570
There was also one leaflet that said “Gentlemen
prefer blondes, but blondes don’t like cripples”-

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:35.120
with a picture of an American veteran amputee.

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:39.610
All of these dark campaigns lead to Sefton
Delmer’s most heartless project yet, called

00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:41.150
“The Dead Letters”.

00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:45.240
British Intelligence was able to intercept
letters written to German soldiers who had

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:46.320
actually died.

00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:49.690
Many of them were from concerned mothers,
saying that they had not heard from their

00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:52.390
sons in a while, and hoped they were safe.

00:15:52.390 --> 00:15:56.170
If British Intelligence managed to intercept
those letters, Delmer would write back to

00:15:56.170 --> 00:15:59.950
these families, claiming that these men were
in hiding, and would be home soon.

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:03.600
At first, this sounds like he actually being
kind to these German families.

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:07.870
But after reading enough of these letters
over the radio, German soldiers who heard

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:12.270
the broadcasts would hear the names of the
men they saw dying in front of their eyes.

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:15.520
They knew that someone was lying, and they
believed that the Dead Letters were coming

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:17.110
from the German government.

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:21.030
During these dark times, Sefton Delmer’s
wife, Isabel, could not take it any longer.

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:25.100
She resented Delmer for how cruel he was being
to his fellow human beings.

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:27.540
War or not, this propaganda wasn’t funny
anymore.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:29.530
She couldn’t handle having any part in it.

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:31.170
They ended up getting a divorce.

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:35.110
The war had left its scars, and Isabel would
go through two more marriages before the end

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:36.160
of her life.

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:39.820
After World War II was over, Sefton Delmer
returned to his job at the Daily Express.

00:16:39.820 --> 00:16:44.690
He published a novel called Black Boomerang
in 1962, but beyond that, he lived out a quiet

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:45.690
retirement.

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:49.820
Sworn to secrecy, he never fully revealed
the details of his time creating Black Propaganda,

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:54.400
until the 1970’s, when enough time had passed,
and he was allowed to finally talk about his

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:57.820
experiences in his autobiography, The Counterfeit
Spy.

00:16:57.820 --> 00:17:02.630
Today, few people remember Sefton Delmer,
or how he was a voice of opposition for the

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:07.680
German people, who were used to hearing the
loud lies of Adolf Hitler and Joseph Goebbels.

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:12.520
While we will never know just how many people
heard his broadcasts, we do know that his

00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:26.699
work was one of the many elements that helped
the Allies win

00:17:26.699 --> 00:17:33.130
the war.

